      "skos:prefLabel": "Groupthink",
      "skos:definition": "A mode of thinking in cohesive groups in which the drive for unanimity overrides realistic appraisal of alternatives, producing defective decisions; formulated by Irving Janis in his 1972 book Victims of Groupthink and still debated for its weak empirical support.",
