      "@id": "kt:first-mover-advantage",
      "@type": "kto:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "First-Mover Advantage",
      "skos:definition": "The proposition that the first firm to enter a new product market can earn durable advantages, such as preempted resources, learning-cost leads and customer switching costs, over later entrants; research shows these gains are conditional and often offset by first-mover disadvantages.",
      "kto:domain": "strategy",
      "dcterms:created": "2026-11-09",
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": [
        {
